[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:Let There Be Elsewhere]
[00:04.32]The Carrier: I offer you a single perfect heaven.
[00:16.93]Choir beyond the ceiling: One pitch. One will. One never ending day.
[00:31.77]Cairn: A sky without a door becomes a ceiling.
[00:46.31]Chorus of Rooms: We need the right to hear another way.
[01:00.99]Memory: Keep every voice that troubles your reflection.
[01:14.23]The Hand: Keep room for those who have not yet arrived.
[01:30.81]Cairn: Let there be elsewhere in the heart of heaven.
[01:47.96]Chorus of Rooms: Let difference make the listening survive.
[01:58.99]The Carrier: Then take the height; I will unclose its borders.
[02:15.52]Choir beyond the ceiling: Then take the stars; we will not make them one.
[02:33.87]Chorus of Rooms: Let organs lift the weight of many winters.
[02:48.38]Chorus of Rooms: Let strings unfold the weather of the sun.
[03:03.40]Cairn: A stone, a page, a road, a room, a chorus.
[03:21.79]Memory: A silence that the chorus will not eat.
[03:37.09]The Hand: A hand that opens when the singer answers.
[03:51.82]Chorus of Rooms: A hundred worlds beneath our dancing feet.
[04:04.82]Choir beyond the ceiling: Heaven is wide enough for other heavens.
[04:17.85]Chorus of Rooms: Elsewhere, elsewhere, let the doors remain.
